Subject: [PATCH] Restore the SM8250 native AOD command and image bridge

The Android 17 donor keeps the native implementations but omits registration
and replaces its Binder entry points with failure stubs. Dispatch supported
commands to the existing implementation without changing the live-clock feature.

Validate the single-panel node and exact command payload sizes before JNI:
1/2: move on/off; 3: time (6 ints); 8: partial HLPM (9 ints);
9: analog v4 (6 ints); 10: digital v4 (16 ints). The older command 6 uses a
four-int analog ioctl which does not match the SM8250 six-int structure.

Check system/SystemUI callers before clearing identity, restore identity on
all paths after clearing it, and serialize the two entry points because JNI
uses shared command buffers. The image-info string is not part of the native
image API. Leave the unused legacy info/needle entry points unchanged.

